you wear the same outfit for a week many  people across the valley do and it's not  by choice one group of women plans to do  just that to draw attention to and spark  a conversation about poverty in our  community junior league of las vegas  will host the little black dress  initiative this week these ladies will  wear the same little black dress for  five days and raise money to help  families in need the goal is to talk  with friends family and co-workers about  this issue and offer ways to give a hand  here in las vegas and in southern nevada  one in six families is below the poverty  line and one in three children face  hunger and  food insecurity issues  hunger and homelessness do not  discriminate it affects women children  veterans uh senior citizens it impacts  people all over our valley and we the  women of junior  league believe it's our duty to commit  and engage and to help people  this year the league wants to raise  twenty five thousand dollars a five  dollar donation can provide meals to a  child for a week and twenty five dollars  can buy a jacket and a hat for a child  in need this winter this week they will  also pack hygiene kits for the shannon  west homeless youth center to learn more  visit ldbi22.givesmart.com
 

